     8    inbox/*.json                   proposals {"kind": ..., "body": ...}; 
CI moves them into entries/
     9  
    10  An entry's identity is the sha256 of its stored bytes, which must be 
exactly its RFC 8785 (JCS) form
    11  (no trailing newline). The rules that make Python's json.dumps output 
equal JCS are enforced: ASCII
    12  keys, no floats, integers within +-(2**53-1), no lone surrogates.
    13  
    14  Commands: ingest | verify | head | range | check-anchors | monitor.
    15  Exit codes: 0 ok; 1 the ledger, an anchor or the monitor's finding is 
wrong; 2 can't check (missing
    16  library or network); 3 unexpected failure. A failure is never reported 
as a verdict.
    17  """
    18  import argparse, base64, datetime, hashlib, json, os, re, subprocess, 
sys, urllib.error, urllib.request
